{#- The Circle: the people it is made of, the screen, and the two moments around it (choosing who you pay for, nudging someone).
    On a narrow screen it is the same collage with the pieces laid over the screen's edges (style.css): --at is where a piece
    sits along the screen's height (start, end or centre), and each is drawn at the size, relative to the screen, it has beside it
    on a wide one. A piece with data-enlarge opens full screen on a tap there (spread-zoom.js), so what is too small to
    read can be read. A piece's image must have a transparent background, as it lies over the white screen there: one exported
    on the mat has #121212 behind it, which scripts/cutout.js takes off. -#}
<div class="collage">
  <div class="collage__l">
    <img data-reveal src="/assets/images/projects/jh/circle-people.png" alt="Four illustrated portraits: an older woman with grey hair, an older man with a grey beard, a girl with bunches and a boy" style="--w: 150; --at: start" sizes="(max-width: 860px) 25vw, 150px">
    <img data-reveal data-enlarge src="/assets/images/projects/jh/circle-reminder.png" alt="A card reading 'Send a reminder: create or edit your SMS', with a Send SMS button and an illustration of a hand holding a phone" style="--w: 288; --at: end" sizes="(max-width: 860px) 25vw, 288px">
  </div>
  <div class="collage__c">
    <img data-enlarge src="/assets/images/projects/jh/circle-phone.png" alt="My Jireh Circle: the user at the centre with four Circle members around them, a Dependants row, and an Add a Circle member button" style="--w: 332" sizes="(max-width: 860px) min(332px, 62vw), 332px">
  </div>
  <div class="collage__r">
    <img data-reveal data-enlarge src="/assets/images/projects/jh/circle-dropdown.png" alt="Who are you paying for? A list of Circle members with their relationship to you: You, Uncle, Friend, Brother, and an Add a dependant row" style="--w: 273; --at: start" sizes="(max-width: 860px) 25vw, 273px">
    <img data-reveal src="/assets/images/projects/jh/circle-mini.png" alt="A person at the centre of a circle, linked to two others" style="--w: 84; --at: end" sizes="(max-width: 860px) 25vw, 84px">
  </div>
</div>
